"substantive"},{"id":"error-handling","title":"Error paths, edge cases, invariants","selectors":["/body/errorPaths"],"concerns":["Is the missing/invalid `at` detection logic (new Date + isNaN) sufficient to cover all cited edge cases (empty string, non-ISO, far-future date)?","Does the fallback behavior (no span, no throw) actually preserve the pre-story markup as claimed, verifiable against current whoRow code?","Are the three stated invariants (at field untouched, parity tests, opposite-end placement without altering row alignment) complete, or is a relevant invariant missing (e.g. CSP/sanitization of the injected webview string)?","Is the edge case table exhaustive for all row kinds that pass through whoRow, and does it correctly exclude non-message rows?"],"dependsOn":["contracts-data-model"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"test-strategy","title":"Test strategy and acceptance mapping","selectors":["/body/testStrategy"],"concerns":["Does every acceptance criterion (ac1-ac3) referenced in the mapping actually exist and trace to a real, nameable test case in the cited test files?","Do the unit and integration test levels adequately cover the contract postconditions and error-path edge cases identified in contracts-data-model and error-handling, with no coverage gap (e.g. parity test between host meta.at and webview at)?","Are the cited fixtures (fake-DOM harness, restored(...) views) real and fit for purpose given the actual test files' structure?","Is test framework identification (node:test via tsx --test) consistent with repo convention?"],"dependsOn":["contracts-data-model","error-handling"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"migration-rollout","title":"Migration, backward compatibility, rollback","selectors":["/body/migration"],"concerns":["Is the 'zero downtime, no data rewrite' claim justified given the data model changes (meta.at is additive-only, at field unmodified)?","Is the rollback story (single-commit revert) realistic given the scope of changed call sites and CSS?","Does the backward-compat claim correctly address old session files with no `at` or malformed `at`, consistent with the error-paths fallback behavior?"],"dependsOn":["contracts-data-model"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"alternatives","title":"Alternatives considered and rationale for chosen a1","selectors":["/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/alternativesConsidered/3"],"concerns":["Are the four alternatives meaningfully distinct and do their pros/cons fairly represent trade-offs against the captured scope/constraints?","Is the rejection rationale for a2/a3/a4 sound and consistent with the chosen a1's actual design in contracts-data-model (e.g. a4's rejection reasoning doesn't contradict a1's final approach)?","Does the chosen alternative (a1) match what sections 2-6 actually describe, with no drift between the alternative's one-line summary and the detailed contract/data-model sections?"],"dependsOn":["scope-summary"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"ux-visual","title":"UX definition and companion mock rendering","selectors":["/body/uxDefinition","/body/companions","document:line:185"],"concerns":["Does the uxDefinition (AdaptiveCard body) accurately depict the opposite-end placement and smaller-font claims made in contracts-data-model, with no mismatch between the mock and the written contract?","Is the companion ux-mock.html file present, non-broken, and does its actual rendering (not just the definition) demonstrate the claimed layout — inspect the real file, don't take the definition as proof?","Is a UX artifact even warranted here given the front-door relevance rule (this is a layout/visual change, so UX mock is appropriate) — confirm it's not over- or under-specified?"],"dependsOn":["contracts-data-model"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"citations-traceability","title":"Citation accuracy and traceability of all code/step-